Background of Study 
Companies collect transactional sales data from multiple sources (POS, e-commerce, ERPs). 
Such raw data often contains inconsistencies, missing values, mixed formats and noise. 
Before performing any analysis—trend detection, dashboarding or modeling—the raw data 
must be cleaned and validated. This document describes the Excel-based cleaning process 
applied to a sample retail sales dataset covering January 1, 2023 through December 31, 
2024 (1500 rows). The goal was to transform messy, real-world data into an analysis-ready 
dataset while documenting every change for reproducibility and client trust. 
 
Aim of Study 
The primary aim of this cleaning project was to convert the raw retail sales dataset into a 
clean, consistent and validated Excel file suitable for analysis and dashboarding. Specific 
objectives include: 
 - Identify and document data quality issues (missing data, inconsistent formats, 
duplicates, outliers). 
 - Apply conservative and explainable imputation methods where necessary, while 
retaining provenance (imputation flags). 
 - Standardize categorical values and data types for accurate aggregation and joins. 
 - Create derived features to support downstream analysis and Power BI dashboarding. 
 
